{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The C control-flow classes are: `fgets` success, EOF, and read error; newline/EOF/13-byte termination; `atoi` zero, sign/whitespace, nonnumeric, embedded NUL, and 32-bit truncation; and `data < 100` on both sides, with `99` as the largest valid copy count. Negative parsed values deliberately enter the C program’s unchecked signed-to-`size_t` path, so the suite will compare the resulting process signal as well as output. The `printLine(NULL)` branch is not input-reachable because both call sites pass concrete arrays or literals.\n\nI’m adding one integration-test harness that always launches both executables, including a directory-backed stdin case to force an actual `fgets` read error."}}
